{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nAfter operation-family cutovers, leaving generic `_call_with_retry`, `_best_effort`, duck-typed production dispatch, or legacy write routes active would preserve retry multiplication and allow future code to bypass the coordinator. Preview/log consumers also need a stable versioned contract for lifecycle and deferred outcomes before expand can contract.\n\n## Outcome\nFinish the expand/contract migration: route every supported live mutation through typed plans/coordinator/adapters, remove obsolete physical-retry and write fallbacks, fail loudly for unsupported production paths, and seal manifests, logs, pass cursor/tallies, documentation, and local verified-fake validation. Preserve existing mutation shape while making lifecycle/retry/fuse outcomes explicit and observable.\n\n## Plan\n1. Inventory every Cloud/DC mutation leaf and prove it reaches the typed coordinator. Remove generic whole-operation retry, `_best_effort` write swallowing, production class-name/duck fallbacks, and duplicate SDK/adapter retry owners.\n2. Keep compatibility only at serialized/public read boundaries. An unsupported live action raises a typed pre-effect error; tests may use explicit fakes implementing the declared protocol.\n3. Finalize versioned preview/manifest sections for lifecycle intents, logical/physical attempts, delay source/value, budgets, scope, disposition, `retry_not_before`, fuse state, and exact per-ticket/pass outcomes. Redact secrets and bound diagnostic size.\n4. Advance cursor/baseline/binding state only for proven postconditions. Deferred, failed, skipped, and commit-unknown work remains eligible for later re-observation and is never reported as applied.\n5. Add ADR/docs for retry ownership, failure taxonomy, scoped fuse, label-first create containment, explicit behavior deltas, expand/contract rollback, and future adapter obligations. Run portable verified-fake Cloud/DC end-to-end tests; retain bounded live probes as optional operator evidence.\n\n## Testing (RED → GREEN)\n- A dispatch census test enumerates every `MutationDirection`/`MutationAction` and provider route, asserting one typed owner or an intentional pre-effect unsupported error.\n- End-to-end fake Cloud/DC passes cover mixed success, transient recovery, long-delay deferral, permanent ticket failure, auth/provider stop, fuse open/reset, create containment, restart, and delivery failure.\n- Golden preview/log/manifest tests pin existing mutation fields plus additive versioned sections, redaction, bounded diagnostics, and exact tally/exit semantics.\n- Static/string and runtime poison tests fail if removed legacy helpers or hidden retries are reachable from production.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nContract only after shadow parity and each family cutover test passes. A pre-contract release can revert per-family routing; after removal, rollback is a code revert that re-observes remote state and never compensates by deleting successful Jira work. Stored ticket/binding/event formats are unchanged; additive manifest fields are versioned and ignorable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A route census proves every supported Cloud/DC mutation uses exactly one typed coordinator/adapter path and no hidden SDK, generic wrapper, `_best_effort`, or duck-typed production fallback remains reachable.\n- [ ] Unsupported production actions fail before local/remote effects with a typed provider-neutral error.\n- [ ] Preview, manifest, and logs preserve existing mutation fields and add versioned redacted logical-attempt, lifecycle, delay/budget, disposition, fuse, and `retry_not_before` data.\n- [ ] Cursor, baseline, and binding state advance only for proven postconditions; deferred/failed/skipped/commit-unknown work is never counted as applied and remains recoverable next pass.\n- [ ] Portable verified-fake Cloud/DC end-to-end suites cover the approved taxonomy, retry envelope, fuse, create containment, restart, and partial-outcome behavior without external credentials.\n- [ ] ADR and operator docs record ownership, intentional behavior changes, future adapter contract, no-dual-write cutover, and rollback that never deletes successful Jira work.\n\n## Inherited invariant — pre-observation repair boundary (folded in from insectile-modest-martin, 2026-08-19)\n\nOperator decision: `insectile-modest-martin` (d7b9-ac42) is CLOSED and its requirement now lives\nhere. This ticket edits `reconcile.py`, which sits at **799 of the 800-line cap**, so it must\nperform a behaviour-preserving extraction (extract along an existing call-graph seam; NEVER raise\nthe limit). That extraction must preserve one specific ordering invariant that is easy to break\nsilently.\n\n**The invariant.** The call\n`binding_store.repair_at_write_boundary(persist=persist, scoped=bool(scoped_ids))` must remain:\n\n- **AFTER** the under-lock staleness validation (`ensure_selection_current`) — a pass whose\n  selection is stale has not established that its view is current and has no standing to repair; and\n- **BEFORE** the pass's first remote issue fetch (`fetcher.fetch_snapshot` / `compute_snapshot`).\n\nThe pre-observation half is the one with teeth. A durable tombstone is authoritative retirement\nintent. A pass that fetched first could observe the retired issue answer 200 and then complete that\nissue's retirement in the same breath as fresh evidence that it is alive; repairing first keeps the\nrecorded decision from racing a later observation. **Move the call after the fetch and the repair\nstill runs, still writes correct-looking bytes, and is silently wrong.**\n\n`run_differs.py` is specifically NOT an alternative home: `reconcile._load_snapshots` performs the\nfirst remote fetch inside itself, and both `bind_operation_runtime` and `run_differs()` run after it\nreturns, so no position inside `run_differs.py` can precede remote observation. Recorded in ADR 0099.\n\n**The two tests that are the only guard** (both drive or name `_load_snapshots` directly, so an\nextraction that renames or re-splits that phase WILL force someone to touch them) — in\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_recovery_write_boundary.py`:\n\n- `test_repair_runs_before_the_first_remote_observation` — the behavioural oracle; drives the real\n  load phase with an event recorder and asserts the repair event precedes the fetch event.\n- `test_the_repair_is_invoked_from_reconcile_and_not_from_run_differs` — a structural anchor.\n\nThe tempting shortcut under time pressure is to relax the assertion rather than re-anchor it.\n**Relaxing it is the thing to avoid.**\n\n### Additional acceptance criteria (inherited)\n- [ ] After this change to `reconcile.py`, the repair call still runs after the under-lock staleness\n      gate and before the pass's first remote issue fetch.\n- [ ] `test_repair_runs_before_the_first_remote_observation` still fails when the call is moved to a\n      post-fetch position — demonstrated by SEEDING that move and observing RED, not merely by the\n      suite being green.\n- [ ] If the load phase is renamed or re-split, the boundary tests are RE-ANCHORED to the new\n      structure rather than relaxed, and the ordering assertion survives in a form that still\n      discriminates.\n- [ ] `reconcile.py` remains within the 800-line cap without raising the limit.\n- [ ] ADR 0099's invocation-boundary section is updated if the realized position changes shape.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787173963936106001,"uuid":"5ab49299-52b1-45f9-b2af-602f5d5ed203"}